„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections–…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£And afterward Moses and Aaron went in, and told Pharaoh, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Let my people go, that they may hold a feast unto me in the wilderness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„And Pharaoh said, Who is the LORD, that I should obey his voice to let Israel go? I know not the LORD, neither will I let Israel go.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÓAnd they said, The God of the Hebrews hath met with us: let us go, we pray thee, three days' journey into the desert, and sacrifice unto the LORD our God; lest he fall upon us with pestilence, or with the sword.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒAnd the king of Egypt said unto them, Wherefore do ye, Moses and Aaron, let the people from their works? get you unto your burdens.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhAnd Pharaoh said, Behold, the people of the land now are many, and ye make them rest from their burdens.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]And Pharaoh commanded the same day the taskmasters of the people, and their officers, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqYe shall no more give the people straw to make brick, as heretofore: let them go and gather straw for themselves.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊAnd the tale of the bricks, which they did make heretofore, ye shall lay upon them; ye shall not diminish ought thereof: for they be idle; therefore they cry, saying, Let us go and sacrifice to our God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkLet there more work be laid upon the men, that they may labour therein; and let them not regard vain words.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book§chapter«first_verse
