¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”And the taskmasters of the people went out, and their officers, and they spake to the people, saying, Thus saith Pharaoh, I will not give you straw.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZGo ye, get you straw where ye can find it: yet not ought of your work shall be diminished.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhSo the people were scattered abroad throughout all the land of Egypt to gather stubble instead of straw.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfAnd the taskmasters hasted them, saying, Fulfil your works, your daily tasks, as when there was straw.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÙAnd the officers of the children of Israel, which Pharaoh's taskmasters had set over them, were beaten, and demanded, Wherefore have ye not fulfilled your task in making brick both yesterday and to day, as heretofore?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThen the officers of the children of Israel came and cried unto Pharaoh, saying, Wherefore dealest thou thus with thy servants?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–There is no straw given unto thy servants, and they say to us, Make brick: and, behold, thy servants are beaten; but the fault is in thine own people.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`But he said, Ye are idle, ye are idle: therefore ye say, Let us go and do sacrifice to the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkGo therefore now, and work; for there shall no straw be given you, yet shall ye deliver the tale of bricks.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡And the officers of the children of Israel did see that they were in evil case, after it was said, Ye shall not minish ought from your bricks of your daily task.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTAnd they met Moses and Aaron, who stood in the way, as they came forth from Pharaoh:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÌand they said unto them, The LORD look upon you, and judge; because ye have made our savour to be abhorred in the eyes of Pharaoh, and in the eyes of his servants, to put a sword in their hand to slay us.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And Moses returned unto the LORD, and said, Lord, wherefore hast thou so evil entreated this people? why is it that thou hast sent me?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚For since I came to Pharaoh to speak in thy name, he hath done evil to this people; neither hast thou delivered thy people at all.¦layout ªlast_verse